Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

&amp;nbsp;






 PRINTERSCLAN





 &amp;nbsp;





 &amp;nbsp;


 &amp;nbsp;



 Dear stan Jablonski We hope this email finds you well.
 We appreciate you reaching out about issues with your
 Canon printer
 MG2522








 Printer Can&#039;t Connect (Windows)





 1. Check to make sure the printer is turned on and
 connected to the same Wi-Fi network as your device.




 To find out if your printer is
 connected to Wi-Fi, see if your printer&#039;s built-in menu has
 options for checking its Wi-Fi connection, or check the
 printer&#039;s manual for instructions about how to add it to a
 Wi-Fi network.







 2. Do a Hard Reset on the Printer




 Sometimes power-cycling your printer
 can resolve the issue. Turn off your printer and unplug it,
 wait 30 seconds, plug your printer back in, and then turn
 the printer back on.







 3. Default Printer





 a) Select Start &gt; Settings &gt; Devices &gt; Printers &amp;
 scanners.
 b) Select your printer as the default printer in the list
 of Printers and scanners.
 If you see a message that says, &quot;Windows will stop
 managing your default printer for you,&quot; select OK.








 4. Clear the Print queue




 a) Select Start &gt; Settings &gt; Devices &gt; Printers &amp;
 scanners.
 b) Select your printer and then select Open queue.
 c) Under Document Name, select any documents listed, then
 select Document, and select Cancel.








 5. Remove and reinstall Printer on your computer




 a) Remove your printer:
 Select Start &gt; Settings &gt; Devices &gt; Printers &amp; scanners.

 Select your printer, select Remove device, and then
 select Yes.
 b) Reinstall your printer:
 Select Start &gt; Settings &gt; Devices &gt; Printers &amp; scanners.

 Make sure your printer is turned on and connected. Select
 Add a printer or scanner and follow the instructions to
 reinstall your printer.








 6. Restart your PC





 Restarting your PC can sometimes help to refresh the
 services and components necessary for your device to
 communicate with your printer.







 Printer Can&#039;t Connect (Mac)




 1. If your printer is connected...




 If your printer is connected to your
 Mac, make sure the printer cable is firmly connected, and
 the printer is plugged into a power point and turned on.








 2. If the printer is on the...




 2. If the printer is on the network,
 make sure your Mac and the printer are still on the same
 network, the printer is turned on, and the network isn’t
 experiencing problems. If the network has multiple printers,
 check which printer you chose — it may be different from the
 one you think you chose.







 3. Add your Printer again-






 a) On your Mac, if the printer is on the network, choose
 Apple menu &gt; System Settings, then click Printers &amp;
 Scanners in the sidebar. (You may have to scroll down.)

 b) Add the printer to your list of available printers:
 Click the Add Printer, Scanner or Fax button on the
 right. A dialogue appears listing printers on your local
 network. It may take a minute or two for your printer to
 appear.
 c) If your printer still doesn’t appear in the list, try
 adding the printer by its IP address.










 &amp;nbsp;





 If your issue is still not resolved or you&#039;re unable to follow these
 instructions, contact our troubleshooting experts, who will diagnose the
 specific problem you&#039;re facing. Our certified experts will help you resolve
 the issue over the phone CALL OUR EXPERTS +1-512-885-1530.










 &amp;nbsp;




 &amp;copy; https://printersclan.com



 &amp;nbsp;


--B_ALT_6779894e534455.87417444
